input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,9885,678,6351,5109,400,89,3,1741,429,198,59,7265,90,6612,9,532,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,19,15170,89,481,220,23,92,1124,1291,91,14581,220,16,11,90155,59,2359,91,1124,37018,90,89,481,220,16,17,15170,89,481,220,23,72,92,1124,1291,91,14581,1124,37018,90,20,15170,18,27275,59,408,90,6612,9,92,6269,678,279,9904,11,18663,553,76602,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nFind all complex numbers $z$ such that\n\\begin{align*}\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| &= 1, \\\\\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| &= \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\end{align*}Enter all the solutions, separated by commas.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5618e45fbb00d0bfe32a1ab22abc3548de9cb2e55a52ab701bfcaafcf1d1ea4c"},"seconds":67.00166082382202,"seed":916815572125939632,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for the complex numbers \\( z \\) that satisfy the given equations, we will analyze each equation separately and then find the intersection of the solutions.\n\nFirst, consider the equation:\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 4}{z - 8} \\right| = 1.\n\\]\nThis implies that the distance from \\( z \\) to 4 is equal to the distance from \\( z \\) to 8. Therefore, \\( z \\) lies on the perpendicular bisector of the line segment joining 4 and 8. The midpoint of 4 and 8 is 6, and the perpendicular bisector is the vertical line \\( x = 6 \\). Thus, \\( z \\) can be written as \\( z = 6 + bi \\) for some real number \\( b \\).\n\nNext, consider the equation:\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{z - 12}{z - 8i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nSubstituting \\( z = 6 + bi \\) into this equation, we get:\n\\[\n\\left| \\frac{(6 + bi) - 12}{(6 + bi) - 8i} \\right| = \\left| \\frac{-6 + bi}{6 + (b-8)i} \\right| = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nThe magnitude of a complex number \\( a + ci \\) is given by \\( \\sqrt{a^2 + c^2} \\). Therefore, we have:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{(-6)^2 + b^2}}{\\sqrt{6^2 + (b-8)^2}} = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nSimplifying the magnitudes, we get:\n\\[\n\\frac{\\sqrt{36 + b^2}}{\\sqrt{36 + (b-8)^2}} = \\frac{5}{3}.\n\\]\nSquaring both sides, we obtain:\n\\[\n\\frac{36 + b^2}{36 + (b-8)^2} = \\frac{25}{9}.\n\\]\nCross-multiplying gives:\n\\[\n9(36 + b^2) = 25(36 + (b-8)^2).\n\\]\nExpanding both sides, we get:\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 900 + 25(b^2 - 16b + 64).\n\\]\nSimplifying further, we have:\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 900 + 25b^2 - 400b + 1600.\n\\]\nRearranging terms, we get:\n\\[\n324 + 9b^2 = 2500 + 25b^2 - 400b.\n\\]\nBringing all terms to one side, we obtain:\n\\[\n0 = 2276 + 16b^2 - 400b.\n\\]\nRearranging gives the quadratic equation:\n\\[\n16b^2 - 400b + 2276 = 0.\n\\]\nDividing the entire equation by 4, we get:\n\\[\n4b^2 - 100b + 569 = 0.\n\\]\nUsing the quadratic formula \\( b = \\frac{-B \\pm \\sqrt{B^2 - 4AC}}{2A} \\) with \\( A = 4 \\), \\( B = -100 \\), and \\( C = 569 \\), we get:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{100 \\pm \\sqrt{10000 - 9104}}{8} = \\frac{100 \\pm \\sqrt{896}}{8} = \\frac{100 \\pm 8\\sqrt{14}}{8} = \\frac{25 \\pm 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}.\n\\]\nThus, the solutions for \\( b \\) are:\n\\[\nb = \\frac{25 + 2\\sqrt{14}}{2} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = \\frac{25 - 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}.\n\\]\nTherefore, the solutions for \\( z \\) are:\n\\[\nz = 6 + \\frac{25 + 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}i \\quad \\text{and} \\quad z = 6 + \\frac{25 - 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}i.\n\\]\nThus, the solutions are:\n\\[\n\\boxed{6 + \\frac{25 + 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}i, 6 + \\frac{25 - 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}i}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{6 + \\frac{25 + 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}i, 6 + \\frac{25 - 2\\sqrt{14}}{2}i}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
